      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Diagnosis of ectopic pregnancy continues to be an important challenge facing emergency physicians. The authors present a case of bilateral tubal ectopic pregnancy and discuss its clinical features and diagnostic difficulties. A review of the English-language literature on the subject is discussed. Suggestions are made on ways to increase diagnostic accuracy, reduce complications, and preserve future fertility in this group of patients."},
